class:: VisualServer
summary:: Pattern-based visual composition server (mirrors the audio server)
categories:: Libraries>VisualServer
related:: Classes/VisualSynthDef, Classes/VisualRenderer, Classes/Vbind, Guides/VisualServer, Reference/VisualParameters

description::

The core of the Visual Server system. It manages link::Classes/UserView:: windows ("views") and visual "nodes", offering a server-like interface (code::vnew::, code::vset::, code::vfree::) analogous to the audio server's code::s_new::/code::n_set::/code::n_free::.

A singleton is available as link::#*default::. Visual nodes are rendered every frame by a per-view draw function; each node's appearance and lifetime are produced by a link::Classes/VisualSynthDef::.

Event types in code::VisualEventTypes.scd:: must be loaded after class compilation for the pattern classes (link::Classes/Vbind:: etc.) to work. See link::Guides/VisualServer::.

code::
v = VisualServer.default;
v.start;
~view = v.createView(\demo, Rect(200, 200, 800, 600));
v.vnew(\circle, nil, \demo, [\x, 0, \y, 0, \size, 80, \color, Color.red]);
::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: default
The shared singleton instance, created in code::*initClass::. This is the server used by the event types and pattern classes by default.

method:: new
Create a new server instance. Normally you use link::#*default:: instead.

method:: visualArgsFrom
Collect the provided shape parameters from an event into a code::[key, value, ...]:: array, used internally by the event types in code::VisualEventTypes.scd::.
argument:: env
The event (environment). Only the event's strong::own:: keys are collected (via code::includesKey::) so that keys inherited from SC's default parent event (notably code::sustain:: as a Function, and code::legato:: 0.8) do not leak into the visual model. Omitted keys fall back to each link::Classes/VisualSynthDef::'s defaults.
discussion::
The collected keys are: code::x y size color dur fill startSize endSize curve x1 y1 x2 y2 width length speed stretch legato sustain attack release::. See link::Reference/VisualParameters::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

private:: init, renderView, renderNode

method:: start
Mark the server running.

method:: stop
Stop the server and free all nodes (calls link::#-freeAll::).

method:: createView
Create a window containing an animated link::Classes/UserView:: that renders this view's nodes at 60 fps.
argument:: name
A link::Classes/Symbol:: identifying the view (e.g. code::\demo::).
argument:: bounds
A link::Classes/Rect::. Default code::Rect(100, 100, 800, 600)::.
argument:: background
A link::Classes/Color::. Default code::Color.black::.
returns:: the link::Classes/UserView::.

method:: vnew
Create a visual node (like code::s_new::).
argument:: defName
The link::Classes/VisualSynthDef:: name, e.g. code::\circle::, code::\pulse::.
argument:: nodeID
An integer id, or code::nil:: to auto-allocate via link::#-nextID::.
argument:: viewName
The view symbol. The view is auto-created if it does not exist.
argument:: args
A flat code::[key, value, ...]:: array of parameters. Values may be link::Classes/Function::s (evaluated every frame — live input).
returns:: the node id.

method:: vset
Set parameters on an existing node (like code::n_set::). Variadic: accepts code::vset(id, \x, 0.5, \color, Color.blue):: or a single array code::vset(id, [\x, 0.5])::.
argument:: nodeID
The node id.

method:: vfree
Free a node (like code::n_free::).
argument:: nodeID
The node id.

method:: nextID
Allocate and return the next node id (starts at 1000).

method:: freeAll
Free every node in every view.

method:: closeAllViews
Close all view windows.

method:: free
Stop the server and close all views.

method:: views
A link::Classes/Dictionary:: of view-name -> view data.

method:: nodes
A link::Classes/Dictionary:: of nodeID -> node event.

method:: isRunning
Boolean run state.

EXAMPLES::

code::
(
(thisProcess.nowExecutingPath.dirname +/+ "VisualEventTypes.scd").load;  // if running from the project
v = VisualServer.default;
v.start;
~view = v.createView(\demo, Rect(200, 200, 800, 600), Color.black);
)

// manual node
~id = v.vnew(\pulse, nil, \demo, [\x, 0, \y, 0, \endSize, 200, \dur, 1.5]);

// live (function) params
v.vnew(\live, nil, \demo, [\x, { 1.0.rand2 }, \y, { 1.0.rand2 }, \dur, inf]);

v.freeAll;
::
